From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:16:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wiki: bring the rest of the event guide's example in line
 with the code

Three details of the worked example in wiki/EventSystem.md do not match
the code it describes:

- The file is src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.cpp, not PortEnhancements.c
  (named in steps 2, 4 and 5).
- REGISTER_LISTENER takes the priority second and the callback last:
  REGISTER_LISTENER(Event, EVENT_PRIORITY_NORMAL, callback). The guide
  had them the other way round, which is not how any call in the tree or
  the snippet in src/port/events/EVENTS.md is written.
- PortEnhancements.cpp registers most listeners as lambdas written in
  place. The guide keeps its named function, which is equally valid (the
  draw-distance listeners are registered that way), and now shows the
  lambda form beside it.

The code fences for the C++ snippets are marked cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
