 wiki/EventSystem.md | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/wiki/EventSystem.md b/wiki/EventSystem.md
index 6bec3416..d8328b0f 100644
--- a/wiki/EventSystem.md
+++ b/wiki/EventSystem.md
@@ -22,11 +22,11 @@ DEFINE_EVENT(RenderPauseCourseOptions,
 ## 2. Register the Event
 The system must register the event ID during the engine's registration phase.
 
-**File:** `src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.c`
+**File:** `src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.cpp`
 
 Add your event to the `PortEnhancements_Register` function:
 
-```c
+```cpp
 void PortEnhancements_Register() {
     // ...
     REGISTER_EVENT(RenderPauseCourseOptions);
@@ -62,9 +62,9 @@ Implement the logic that reacts to the event. This is usually where you check a
 
 Read a setting through the feature registry (`Port_FeatureInt`), not through its CVar. A romhack or mod can disable a feature or force its value, and only a read through the registry honours that; see [Feature rules](../docs/romhacks/DESIGN.md#feature-rules). A new setting also needs its row in `sDefs` in `src/port/features/Features.cpp`.
 
-**File:** `src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.c`
+**File:** `src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.cpp`
 
-```c
+```cpp
 void OnRenderPauseCourseOptions(IEvent* event) {
     // Only apply the logic if the feature is enabled
     if (Port_FeatureInt("cheats.pause_exit_whenever", 0) == 0) {
@@ -84,17 +84,25 @@ void OnRenderPauseCourseOptions(IEvent* event) {
 ## 5. Register the Listener
 Finally, tell the system to execute your callback when the event is triggered.
 
-**File:** `src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.c`
+**File:** `src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.cpp`
 
-Inside `PortEnhancements_Init`, use `REGISTER_LISTENER`:
+Inside `PortEnhancements_Init`, use `REGISTER_LISTENER`. The priority comes second, the callback last:
 
-```c
+```cpp
 void PortEnhancements_Init() {
     // ...
-    REGISTER_LISTENER(RenderPauseCourseOptions, OnRenderPauseCourseOptions, EVENT_PRIORITY_NORMAL);
+    REGISTER_LISTENER(RenderPauseCourseOptions, EVENT_PRIORITY_NORMAL, OnRenderPauseCourseOptions);
 }
 ```
 
+The callback can also be written in place as a lambda, which is how `PortEnhancements.cpp` registers most of its listeners:
+
+```cpp
+REGISTER_LISTENER(RenderPauseCourseOptions, EVENT_PRIORITY_NORMAL, [](IEvent* event) {
+    // ...
+});
+```
